TEXT -248 152 Left 2 ;See file:\nMeasurement_CB_Strom_1sys_second_line_grounded.wxmx\nfor the measurment of CEequivalent and Ipet and Lpet
TEXT 32 16 Left 2 ;NOTE: The cap. current from the CE's of line2\nis zero because the line is grounded.\nSince there is also a cap. coupling from line1\nphase 1,2,3 to line2 phases 1,2,3 now to earth \nmore current flows from line1 to line2 and therefore more current\nflows to the earth. The equivalent CE is now\neven higher as for the open line2 circuit 9.029nF\n(81% of double line circuit)
TEXT -544 64 Left 2 ;NOTE:\nFor transient simulation\nyou have to change the\nvoltage source model to\nv_3phase !!
TEXT 32 96 Left 2 ;The cap. Value to earth of the phases are as follows:\nPhase1: 5.1nF (see as waveform: I(u2:C_10a)/V(n002)/314.159\nPhase2: 4.28nF (see as waveform: I(u2:C_20a)/V(n005)/314.159\nPhase3: 7.3nF (see as waveform: I(u2:C_30a)/V(n008)/314.159\nAverage: 5.56nF
TEXT -496 176 Left 2 ;NOTE: You can see that at the resonant\npoint the starpoint voltage is far\nto high (even higher as the nominal system \nvoltage)\nThis is due to the big differences of the\nreactances of the different phases!\nTherefore the phases needs to be crossed out (transposed)\nSee file Petersen_2sys_crossedout.asc
